codex
The alternate covariance mode is added behind `WB_COVGATE=2`. I’m comparing analytic-only modes now to avoid spending extra MC compute while judging the moment model.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "for mode in 0 1 2; do printf 'COVGATE=%s analytic\\n' \""'$mode"; WB_ANALYTIC_ONLY=1 WB_COVGATE=$mode python eval_client.py | tail -n 2; done' in /opt/tiger/discover/workspace
